{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pCNaggtNYAYecjMr4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleted torrents can no longer get stuck in the resume list, and a profile that already has a stale entry fixes itself on the next resume. The full `npm test`, which includes lint, passes: 4242 of 4242.\n\nAll four changes are in `src/renderer/controllers/torrent-list-controller.js`:\n\n1. **Delete one:** `deleteTorrent` now takes the deleted torrent's info hash out of `state.saved.torrentsToResume`.\n2. **Delete all:** `deleteAllTorrents` empties the list.\n3. **Resume:** `resumePausedTorrents` clears the list *before* it starts resuming anything, so the list is reset even if one resume throws. It also skips any hash that no longer matches a torrent, so it no longer crashes on a missing torrent and the rest of the list gets resumed.\n4. **Prioritize:** `prioritizeTorrent` only adds a hash that isn't already in the list. In practice a duplicate came from the user restarting a paused torrent by hand and then playing again, so the test covers that sequence.\n\nThere's one new test file, `test/unit/torrent-list-resume.js`, with one test per item, each seen failing before its fix. It builds the controller under a `.resume-test.js` suffix so it can't collide with `torrent-context-menu.js`, which builds the same controller with different stubs. I ran the two files together in both orders and both passed. I added a line about that suffix to `test/AGENTS.md`.\n\nOne judgement call: I read \"always resets the list, even if resuming one entry fails\" as \"the reset happens before any resume\". So if an existing torrent throws partway through, the entries after it are not resumed in that pass; I didn't add a catch around each entry. A missing torrent, which was the actual bug, can't cause that any more. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed.\n\nThere are five commits, one per item plus the `test/AGENTS.md` note, and nothing was pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":73292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55616538-4c31-46ba-9fbd-f70a6c9818fa","uuid":"8fc34717-6b63-4269-ba55-778df62c5910","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:13:05.393Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pCNJomESwZaxLEpETz"}
